# The KiCad commit whose api/proto tree is vendored in this directory.
#
# KICAD_COMMIT is the exact commit: it is what scripts/sync-protos.sh fetches and what its --check
# mode verifies against, so the vendored copies never drift, whatever the ref does upstream.
# KICAD_REF is the tag or branch that commit was taken from, kept for humans and for the guard in
# the script: a tag must still resolve to KICAD_COMMIT (an upstream tag that moves is an error), and
# a branch that has moved on is only reported, because the pin is the commit, not the branch.
#
# Prefer a release tag: the generated client speaks the wire format of one KiCad version, and a tag
# is the only ref a user's KiCad build can be matched against. A branch is acceptable when the API
# work this library needs is merged upstream but not yet tagged, pinned at one commit, and moved to
# the release tag as soon as one exists. This is that case: master builds as 10.99.0 and is the
# 11.0 line; it carries the library-table commands, embedded files, design variants, jobs, rules
# and cross-probe messages that no tag has yet (the 10.99.0 tag dates from March 2026 and predates
# all of them). See issue #47.
#
# To move the pin: edit both lines, run scripts/sync-protos.sh, and commit the result.
KICAD_REF=master
KICAD_COMMIT=965fb68075b53cd4eaf2244954c9ef54ae0b433c
